Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: npu: preserve RX buffer ownership for partial packets

A packet can span multiple NPU descriptors. If a later descriptor is not
DONE, freeing the partially assembled skb recycles its buffers while the
ring tail and queued count still reference them. A subsequent poll or ring
cleanup can then reuse or release buffers no longer owned by the ring.

Check the entire descriptor chain before constructing an skb. Observe DMA
ownership before reading packet metadata, and leave an incomplete chain
untouched for the next poll. Keep NPU acceleration enabled.

This fixes the partial-completion error path; a causal connection to the
XR1710G PCIe timeout observed on hardware has not yet been established.

--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -67,18 +67,32 @@
 	int i, nframes, index = q->tail;
 	struct sk_buff *skb = NULL;
 
+	if (!q->queued ||
+	    !(READ_ONCE(desc[index].ctrl) & NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK))
+		return NULL;
+
+	/* The device publishes packet metadata before handing over ownership. */
+	dma_rmb();
 	nframes = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_PKT_COUNT_MASK, desc[index].info);
 	nframes = max_t(int, nframes, 1);
+	if (nframes > q->queued)
+		return NULL;
+
+	/* Keep every buffer owned by the ring until the whole packet is ready.
+	 * Freeing a partial skb would recycle pages still referenced by q->tail.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < nframes; i++) {
+		if (!(READ_ONCE(desc[index].ctrl) & NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK))
+			return NULL;
+		index = (index + 1) % q->ndesc;
+	}
+	dma_rmb();
+	index = q->tail;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < nframes; i++) {
 		struct mt76_queue_entry *e = &q->entry[index];
 		int len = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_CUR_LEN_MASK,
 				    desc[index].ctrl);
-
-		if (!FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK, desc[index].ctrl)) {
-			dev_kfree_skb(skb);
-			return NULL;
-		}
 
 		dma_sync_single_for_cpu(dev->dma_dev, e->dma_addr[0],
 					e->dma_len[0],
